Wands of draining can be generated elsewhere (Gnolls, often).

Now, you can also use the good old Nethack way of learning:
try, die, learn.

It may seem harsh, but YMMV. Someone can find drain resistance a must have  
and someone can do without.
My own priorities both in Nethack and Slash'em have evolved as I changed  
my playstyle...
Some things which I considered useless become more and more useful.
Maybe you'll find out drain resistance to be not that useful given your  
playstyle, maybe you'll find it pretty valuable.

[my first Slash'em ascencion was a monk, hence no DR out of the guild (no  
armor). My second was a knight, hence DR via Exaclibur]

